# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reverse-engineering artifacts (IDA Pro exports / extracted vendor binaries).
# All regenerable from the binaries and never committed. The hand-curated
# datasets under <tool>/extracted/ ARE tracked and preserved via the negations.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# IDA Pro databases
*.i64
*.idb
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.nam
*.til

# Per-target IDA sidecar exports  (<tool>/<tool>_<kind>.json | .dot | .c | .bin)
*_functions.json
*_callgraph.json
*_callgraph.dot
*_ctree.json
*_xrefs.json
*_rtti.json
*_structures.json
*_enums.json
*_switches.json
*_segments.json
*_imports.json
*_prototypes.json
*_comments.json
*_entries.json
*_fixups.json
*_frames.json
*_tryblks.json
*_data_tables.json
*_problems.json
*_metadata.json
*_full.c
*_rodata.bin
*_names.json
*_strings.json
# …but keep the curated ptxas extraction datasets (intentionally tracked)
!ptxas/extracted/*_names.json
!ptxas/extracted/*_strings.json

# Extracted / decompiled output trees (any tool, any depth)
context/
decompiled/
disasm/
graphs/
ida_run_logs/
# Raw extracted vendor packages, IDA exports, and intermediate carve trees for
# neuronx-gpsimd (~11 GB of vendor binaries + IDA sidecars that must never be
# staged). Scoped to neuronx-gpsimd/ so the curated ptxas/extracted/ datasets and
# their !-negations near the top of this file are left completely untouched.
neuronx-gpsimd/extracted/
neuronx-gpsimd/ida/
neuronx-gpsimd/archives/
neuronx-gpsimd/binwalk/
neuronx-gpsimd/knowledge/

# Mined research data (local only)
raw/
findings/
/firmware/
/firmware_6000/
some_docs/

# Extracted target binaries (do not commit vendor binaries)
*.backup
/cicc/cicc
/ptxas/ptxas
/cudafe++/cudafe++
/tileiras/tileiras
